<title>AUSTRALIA: Biggest gains/falls for ASX 100 index in last year.</title>
<headline>Biggest gains/falls for ASX 100 index in last year.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is a list of the 10 largest gaining and falling stocks for Australian companies included in the Australian Stock Exchange's ASX 100 index for the year to May 30.</p>
<p>Top 10 largest gains in year</p>
<p>Rank Name		    Price   pct change</p>
<p> 1   Oil Search	     3.29    157.27</p>
<p> 2   Wesfarmers	    12.20     62.02</p>
<p> 3   Flc-Energy Div	 4.20     61.54</p>
<p> 4   CSL Limited	    8.05     61.00</p>
<p> 5   Natl Aust Bank	18.78     59.83</p>
<p> 6   Transurban Group   988.00     58.97</p>
<p> 7   Sthn Pac Pete	  3.65     58.70</p>
<p> 8   Howard Smith	  11.80     58.60</p>
<p> 9   A N Z Bank	     8.99     56.08</p>
<p>10   Hardie Inds	    4.00     55.64</p>
<p>Top 10 largest falls in year</p>
<p>Rank Name		    Price   pct change</p>
<p> 1   Acacia Resources     1.93    -42.73</p>
<p> 2   Sons Of Gwalia	 5.49    -42.20</p>
<p> 3   Newcrest Mining	3.27    -41.19</p>
<p> 4   Great Central	  2.55    -36.88</p>
<p> 5   Davids Limited	 1.24    -35.75</p>
<p> 6   Plutonic Rsc	   4.81    -35.44</p>
<p> 7   Goldfields	     2.17    -30.00</p>
<p> 8   Normandy Min	   1.61    -27.48</p>
<p> 9   Centaur Min&amp;Expl     1.57    -21.11</p>
<p>10   Burns,Philp &amp; Co     1.93    -20.58</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 373-1800</p>
</text>
